 "interpretation": "Stock: KC/MBON/DAN/APL/DPM reach >=90% of the 50 Hz ceiling within ~17 steps and stay there; removing synapses onto sensory neurons (sensory_input=False) does NOT relieve it, so the attractor is intrinsic to recurrent central-brain / KC excitation (KC->KC 1.15 M ACh synapses) with no refractoriness. A 20 ms refractory breaks the one-spike-per-step lock (KCg-d 16.8 Hz, 67% of the new ceiling) but KC activity stays tonic and input-insensitive; longer refractories lower rates to 2-3 Hz (~27% of ceiling). Strengthening existing APL output 5x on top of 20 ms sparsens KCs to ~1.3 Hz and makes KCg-d visually selective (+7 to +13%), but MBON/DAN activity is then driven mostly by non-KCg-d inputs, so the 418 KCg-d edges carry only ~6-8% of target-MBON output.",
